{id:'loc-tofr-52127',title:'Gloria Vanderbilt Cooper',maker:'Toni Frissell',date:'1966',accession:'tofr.52127',medium:'Photograph made for Vogue',credit:'Toni Frissell Collection, Library of Congress Prints and Photographs Division',image:'https://tile.loc.gov/storage-services/service/pnp/tofr/52100/52127v.jpg',caption:'The frame is not neutral delivery: pose, setting, crop, light, garment, commission, and publication context combine to manufacture a public fashion meaning.',alt:'Gloria Vanderbilt Cooper photographed by Toni Frissell for Vogue in 1966.',url:'https://www.loc.gov/resource/tofr.52127/',license:'Free to Use and Reuse / Library of Congress curated set'},
{id:'81630',title:'Ball gown',maker:'House of Worth',date:'ca. 1887',accession:'1977.292.2a, b',medium:'Silk, glass, metallic thread',credit:'Gift of Agnes de Mille, 1977',image:'https://images.metmuseum.org/CRDImages/ci/web-large/1977.292.2ab_F.jpg',caption:'Materials such as silk, glass, and metallic thread make skilled transformation visible while the museum record still names only the house as maker.',alt:'House of Worth ball gown from about 1887, with a structured pale silk silhouette and elaborate surface ornament.',url:'https://www.metmuseum.org/art/collection/search/81630',license:'Public Domain / Met Open Access'},
{id:'159303',title:'Walking suit',maker:'House of Worth',date:'ca. 1889',accession:'2009.300.73a, b',medium:'Silk',credit:'Brooklyn Museum Costume Collection at The Metropolitan Museum of Art; Gift of the Princess Viggo in accordance with the wishes of the Misses Hewitt, 1931',image:'https://images.metmuseum.org/CRDImages/ci/web-large/31.30a-b_front_CP4.jpg',caption:'A finished suit can preserve the house name while leaving the cutters, fitters, stitchers, finishers, and production negotiations unnamed.',alt:'Dark silk House of Worth walking suit from about 1889, photographed frontally against a neutral background.',url:'https://www.metmuseum.org/art/collection/search/159303',license:'Public Domain / Met Open Access'},
{id:'159172',title:'Ensemble',maker:'House of Worth',date:'1893',accession:'2009.300.620a–e',medium:'Silk, jet, metal',credit:'Brooklyn Museum Costume Collection at The Metropolitan Museum of Art; Gift of Edith Gardiner, 1926',image:'https://images.metmuseum.org/CRDImages/ci/web-large/26.368a-b_front_CP4.jpg',caption:'The ensemble carries material decisions across components; the surviving object cannot narrate every demonstration, correction, and embodied judgment that produced them.',alt:'House of Worth ensemble from 1893 in dark silk with jet and metal ornament, shown frontally.',url:'https://www.metmuseum.org/art/collection/search/159172',license:'Public Domain / Met Open Access'}
