    platform:['LONG VIDEO — Begin with the sentence “send it to production.” Expand it into specification, labor, sample, approval, money, change, shipment, quality, remedy, and archive. Use the public agreement only as one example; label every private arrangement unresolved until evidenced.','SHORT 01 — “Production does not execute vision. People translate it.” Put a decision, a constraint, and a bearer of risk behind every transformation.','SHORT 02 — “The purchase order is not the whole workplace.” Add employer, contractor, subcontractor, worker, jurisdiction, classification evidence, safety route, and payment record.','CAROUSEL — VISION / SPECIFICATION / PATTERN / SAMPLE / MATERIAL / LABOR / APPROVAL / CHANGE / PAYMENT / QUALITY / REMEDY / MEMORY.','NEWSLETTER — Subject: Who actually carries the vision into production? Offer a one-style trace and explain why a house must record uncertainty instead of implying supply-chain knowledge it does not possess.','PARTICIPANT REVIEW — Separate studio, supplier, and worker-facing review sheets so each party can correct role, timeline, decision, cost, safety, confidentiality, and unresolved disagreement.']
