Object.assign(exhibitions,{
  B10:{
    kicker:'Foundation study · Visibility → capacity',
    thesis:'A personal brand makes a person recognizable. An institution makes their judgment, relationships, records, rights, and work capable of operating beyond constant personal performance.',
    intro:['A personal brand can be powerful: a recognizable voice, a face, a promise, and a route through crowded attention. But recognition is not infrastructure. An institution begins where public identity is joined to repeatable decisions, accountable roles, retrievable evidence, controlled assets, and a method for continuing when the founder is unavailable.','The distinction matters in fashion because the public often encounters a name before it encounters the atelier, contracts, archive, production network, or governance behind it. FIT oral histories and archival finding aids preserve precisely the layers publicity tends to compress: formation, collaborators, operating choices, and records. This exhibition treats brand as an interface and institution as the system beneath it.'],
    movements:[
      ['01 · SIGNAL','What does the public recognize?','Identify the repeated promise, visual language, subject, and point of view that make the person legible. These signals matter, but they are evidence of recognition—not proof that the work can be produced, governed, or continued.','INFERENCE',['S11','S13']],
      ['02 · SYSTEM','What repeats without performance?','Map how research becomes a brief, how decisions are approved, how work is produced, and how quality is reviewed. A system must be inspectable enough to improve and flexible enough to accommodate judgment.','PROPOSAL',['S08','S39']],
      ['03 · ASSET','What remains under accountable control?','Separate reputation from the name, entity, marks, domains, mailing list, contracts, files, samples, and archive. The public may perceive one identity while ownership and access are fragmented across many records.','PROPOSAL',['S28','S32']],
      ['04 · ABSENCE','What happens when the founder is offline?','Run a seventy-two-hour absence test. Can collaborators find current files, communicate with clients, fulfill obligations, protect accounts, and identify who may decide? The gaps reveal where a brand still depends on continuous personal availability.','PROPOSAL',['S08','S39']]
    ],
    tension:'Institutionalization can turn a living voice into bureaucracy. The aim is not to make the person interchangeable; it is to protect the conditions that let singular judgment remain singular without making exhaustion the operating model.',
    fieldwork:['Write the public promise in one sentence.','Name the repeatable system that fulfills that promise.','List the controlled record or asset supporting each step.','Run the seventy-two-hour founder-absence test.'],
    objectId:'81112',objectUse:'The House of Worth object record separates recognizable house attribution from the durable cataloguing apparatus that lets the attribution remain useful generations later.',
    outputs:['Canonical essay: Brand Is the Door, Not the House','Eight-minute visual essay script','Nine-frame brand-versus-institution carousel','Three 45-second social scripts','Brand / Institution Gap Audit','Newsletter and LinkedIn editions'],
    platform:['LONG — Open on a founder posting from a fitting room; move beneath the image into roles, records, assets, and an absence test. Close: build a system that protects the eye, not a machine that replaces it.','SHORT 01 — Hook: If your business stops when you stop posting, you have recognition—not yet an institution. Demonstrate the four-layer test in 45 seconds.','SHORT 02 — Show one name splitting into five records: mark, domain, list, archive, agreement. End with the question: which one do you actually control?','CAROUSEL — Nine frames: signal; system; asset; authority; archive; access; absence; gap; first repair.','NEWSLETTER — A 1,200-word field edition with the complete 72-hour test and a downloadable audit.','LINKEDIN — Lead with the operating distinction, give one fashion example, and invite readers to name the task that cannot move without them.']
  },
  CA10:{
    kicker:'Credit study · Signature → constellation',
    thesis:'The lone fashion genius is a useful publicity device and a poor description of how collections acquire form, finish, circulation, and memory.',
    intro:['A collection may be signed by one name, but it is carried through pattern cutting, textile development, sampling, fitting, casting, styling, production, photography, distribution, conservation, and criticism. The problem is not that a creative director has no singular role. The problem is that singular authority is too often narrated as solitary making.','Institutional archives complicate that story. Finding aids, oral histories, accession records, credits, and production documents can reconnect work to the people and relationships that made it possible. This exhibition asks readers to treat credit as operational evidence: a record of who held which knowledge, who made which decision, and where the institution would fracture if that contribution disappeared.'],
    movements:[
      ['01 · SIGNATURE','Why does one name dominate?','A single name gives press, commerce, and memory a compact handle. It can truthfully identify creative authority while still concealing the distributed labor required to materialize that authority.','INFERENCE',['S11','S12','S13']],
      ['02 · CONSTELLATION','Who translated the idea?','Build a role map from concept to archive. Record not only names but decisions: who interpreted proportion, solved construction, negotiated feasibility, shaped the image, and preserved the evidence.','PROPOSAL',['S15','S16','S17']],
      ['03 · CREDIT','What should the record retain?','Credits should travel with garments, images, video, collection notes, and archival deposits. The durable record needs consistent role language and a correction path when work is omitted or misdescribed.','PROPOSAL',['S10','S15']],
      ['04 · POWER','Does visibility follow value?','Credit cannot by itself repair inequitable pay, ownership, or authority. It does, however, make labor and decision structures more legible—creating evidence for harder questions about compensation and control.','INFERENCE',['S10','S15']]
    ],
    tension:'Replacing one heroic story with an indiscriminate list can flatten responsibility. A useful credit system distinguishes creative authority, execution, approval, contribution, and ownership rather than pretending every role is identical.',
    fieldwork:['Choose one finished look.','Trace every decision and hand from research to publication.','Attach a name and role to each decision where consent permits.','Record missing, disputed, or uncredited labor as unresolved.'],
    objectId:'157996',objectUse:'The Jeanne Hallée dress retains a maker name while the record also preserves institution, donor, materials, date, accession, and photography—an entry point into the broader constellation behind survival.',
    outputs:['Canonical essay: The Signature and the Constellation','Ten-minute narrated credit-map script','Seven-role carousel','Four collaborator-credit shorts','Constellation Mapper','Interview, newsletter, and classroom editions'],
    platform:['LONG — Follow one look backward from museum record to the absent production floor; distinguish creative authority from solitary manufacture.','SHORT 01 — A rapid roll call of the decisions hidden inside “designed by.”','SHORT 02 — Ask: if this person vanished from the record, what knowledge would the house lose?','CAROUSEL — Seven role plates with a decision, evidence field, and credit verb on each.','AUDIO — A six-question collaborator oral-history prompt with consent and correction language.','CLASSROOM — Map one object without inventing missing names; label the gaps as part of the evidence.']
  },
  CO06:{
    kicker:'Platform study · Reach → dependency',
    thesis:'A million followers can create extraordinary reach while remaining a rented route to people—subject to platform rules, access loss, algorithmic distribution, and incomplete portability.',
    intro:['Follower count is a visible measure inside a platform. It is not a deed to an audience, a complete customer record, or a guaranteed line of communication. Creators and fashion founders often build real cultural and economic value on accounts whose administration, recovery, distribution, and export are governed elsewhere.','The practical response is not to abandon platforms. It is to treat them as powerful channels inside a broader institutional architecture: an owned domain, consented contact records, documented account authority, retrievable content, customer records where lawfully held, and a tested recovery plan. “Rented” is an operating metaphor here, not a legal classification of every platform relationship.'],
    movements:[
      ['01 · REACH','What can the platform do exceptionally well?','Discovery, social proof, conversation, cultural participation, and rapid distribution are real institutional advantages. The audit begins by naming that value rather than treating dependency as failure.','INFERENCE',['S33','S36']],
      ['02 · ACCESS','Who can enter and recover the account?','Record the account owner, administrators, authentication method, recovery contacts, device access, and escalation route. A display name or founder face does not prove operational control.','PROPOSAL',['S08','S39']],
      ['03 · PORTABILITY','What can leave with consent and context?','Map content originals, captions, contacts, customer records, permissions, analytics exports, and conversation history. Preserve only what may lawfully and ethically be retained.','PROPOSAL',['S08','S39']],
      ['04 · ROUTE','How many ways can the institution reach people?','Build at least one controlled destination and one consent-based contact route. Redundancy should improve continuity without manipulating audiences or copying data beyond its stated purpose.','PROPOSAL',['S08','S39']]
    ],
    tension:'Calling platforms “rented” can understate the communities, creativity, and livelihoods built there. The argument is narrower: meaningful participation and asset control are different institutional questions, and both deserve deliberate design.',
    fieldwork:['List every platform and its actual owner or administrator.','Test recovery without relying on one person or device.','Inventory exportable content and consented contact routes.','Create a continuity notice that does not pressure people to migrate.'],
    objectId:'106420',objectUse:'This dress survives through an institutional record rather than a volatile feed. Its persistent identifier, materials, date, credit, and canonical source model the kind of context platform posts often lose.',
    outputs:['Canonical essay: A Million Followers Is a Rented Institution','Six-minute platform-dependency film script','Eight-frame reach-versus-control carousel','Three account-continuity shorts','Audience Portability Map','Newsletter, LinkedIn, and workshop editions'],
    platform:['LONG — Begin with a seven-digit counter; remove it layer by layer until only access, records, permissions, and routes remain.','SHORT 01 — Followers are reach. They are not automatically contact permission, customer records, or recovery control.','SHORT 02 — The five-minute account continuity drill: owner, admin, recovery, originals, alternate route.','CAROUSEL — Reach; access; data; permission; archive; route; recovery; next action.','WORKSHOP — Complete the portability map without downloading or repurposing personal data beyond consent.','NEWSLETTER — Pair the argument with an account-recovery checklist and a plain-language privacy note.']
  },
  CO08:{
    kicker:'Authorship study · Influence → evidence',
    thesis:'Taste can be recognized, taught, imitated, and commercially valuable without becoming a single ownable legal object; generative AI makes the need to separate those categories urgent.',
    intro:['“Taste” bundles together judgment, selection, arrangement, references, recurring codes, reputation, and the ability to decide what does not belong. Some outputs, names, designs, agreements, and confidential materials may engage specific legal regimes. An aesthetic resemblance or prompt that invokes a style does not by itself answer which right—if any—has been implicated.','WIPO’s fashion resources distinguish trademarks, designs, copyright, and patents as different tools with different subject matter. That is the beginning of the analysis, not a verdict on a particular model, dataset, output, jurisdiction, or dispute. This exhibition offers an evidence architecture: document sources, human decisions, permissions, transformations, claims, and uncertainty before reaching for the word ownership.'],
    movements:[
      ['01 · TASTE','What exactly is being claimed?','Separate a general sensibility from a named mark, protected work, registered design, confidential process, contractual promise, or misleading commercial representation. Precision prevents cultural grievance from being mistaken for a settled legal result.','VERIFIED',['S28','S30','S31']],
      ['02 · TRACE','What entered the process?','Keep a source log for references, licensed assets, model and tool versions, prompts, human selections, rejected outputs, edits, and final approvals. The record supports accountability without proving a legal conclusion on its own.','PROPOSAL',['S08','S39']],
      ['03 · TRANSFORM','Where is human judgment visible?','Describe the problem, constraints, alternatives, selection criteria, arrangement, revision, and final expressive choices. Avoid claiming that effort alone creates protection; the purpose is to preserve an accurate creative record.','PROPOSAL',['S28','S29']],
      ['04 · REVIEW','Which question needs counsel or permission?','Flag identifiable source works, living artists or houses named in prompts, confidential inputs, deceptive attribution, commercial marks, uncertain licenses, and jurisdiction-specific design questions for qualified review.','PROPOSAL',['S28','S29','S30']]
    ],
    tension:'Documentation can become performative transparency, and legal categories cannot resolve every ethical question about extraction, cultural authority, labor, or consent. A responsible process needs both legal review and editorial judgment.',
    fieldwork:['Define the element you are calling taste.','Separate facts, influences, protected assets, and interpretations.','Record inputs, permissions, human decisions, and transformations.','Send unresolved rights or attribution questions to qualified counsel.'],
    objectId:'83877',objectUse:'The maker of this richly documented dress remains identified only as French. The object demonstrates how evidence can preserve material facts while authorship and institutional identity remain unresolved.',
    outputs:['Canonical essay: Can Taste Be Owned?','Twelve-minute evidence-led video script','Ten-frame rights-versus-resemblance carousel','Five AI authorship shorts','Taste Trace Ledger','Newsletter, seminar, and counsel-prep editions'],
    platform:['LONG — Move from the seductive sentence “they stole my taste” to seven narrower questions evidence can actually answer.','SHORT 01 — Style, trademark, copyrighted work, design right, contract, and attribution are not synonyms.','SHORT 02 — Show the trace ledger: source; permission; prompt; selection; edit; approval; unresolved issue.','CAROUSEL — Ten distinctions, each with “what it can show” and “what it cannot decide.”','SEMINAR — Compare one historical reference chain and one generative workflow without reproducing disputed source material.','COUNSEL PREP — Package exact assets, territories, dates, agreements, uses, and desired remedies; do not arrive with only screenshots and conclusions.']
  }
});

